{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are","id":1544459,"title":"Are You Meant to Care What Your Stats Are?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Curseborne"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-22T06:26:57-07:00","id":1544459,"title":"Are You Meant to Care What Your Stats Are?","content":"I mentioned this briefly in the thread on which characters people are making first but looking at the full system, the only way I can make it make sense is if I assume that I'm literally not meant to care what my character's Skills and Attributes are beyond the in-the-moment choices of where to assign the dots I get from Paths. <br /> <br /> As I read the system, Paths (even Role Paths) are (a) intentionally designed as a closed list and (b) meant to be chosen based on what they represent in-world, not on the stats they give you. <br /> <br /> Soft evidence for this comes from the Ashcan characters who all have the from-list option that broadly maps to their character concept. Cassie has &quot;Investigator&quot;, not a custom Role for &quot;Lawyer&quot; and Izzy has &quot;Student&quot; even though she's mechanically primarily a combat character. <br /> <br /> Through this lens the system does *work* but it feels increasingly like having Attributes and Skills at all is almost a legacy feature in that case.<br /> <br /> Of course you can go the other way and only focus on what Attributes and Skills you want but then you're ignoring everything about your character you're meant to invest in and also ignoring the plain text of the character creation system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T11:57:58-07:00","id":1544479,"title":"","content":"I often find myself worried if I've got to roll a dicepool of less than 5 dice. But that might just be me.<br /> <br /> Often times as a player, I will be trying to figure out if I can certain Skill + Attributes in order to make sure I'm not ruining a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T12:57:57-07:00","id":1544487,"title":"","content":"Yeah 5-6 dice is kind of my comfort zone as well. Given how many Attribute points you get, it's pretty easy to get a character who can have a dice pool of 5+ in a wide range of things. What's slightly weird is that the game doesn't give you a huge amount of control over *which* things.<br /> <br /> If I play a Hyde, then I *must* have at least 9 of my 16 Skill points in some combination of Enigmas, Leadership, Science, Athletics, Close Combat and Survival. I have to have at least 6 dots in Mental Attributes and 5 in Physical. My Social Attribute pool maxes out at 6 and then only if I am *specifically* an Influencer.<br /> <br /> What I'm struggling with is whether this is a bug or a feature. Obviously it's a radical departure from previous games, even previous Storypath games but I do also want to give it a fair shake. Although the title of this thread is a teensy bit hyperbolic I do think that the system *seems* to want you to view your character's Attributes and Skills almost as something you discover during character creation, rather than something you deliberately aim towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T14:16:11-07:00","id":1544499,"title":"","content":"Whether you care is really in the eye of the beholder. But you can adjust your Attributes each session. That's what the Tweaks part of character creation is for. Your first session is your baseline. Your character is malleable from there. So as you discover the kind of character you are, you tailor your Attribute to suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T16:02:09-07:00","id":1544512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544499#post1544499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whether you care is really in the eye of the beholder. But you can adjust your Attributes each session. That's what the Tweaks part of character creation is for. Your first session is your baseline. Your character is malleable from there. So as you discover the kind of character you are, you tailor your Attribute to suit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay but is that not a *very* roundabout way of doing it?<br /> <br /> I'm glad Tweaks are a thing because I do actually think Develop In Play is an important approach to support but it seems weird if they're the intended to be a major part of character customisation.<br /> <br /> This would seem to imply that the actual intended design of the game is that I have to play multiple sessions in order to create the character I wanted at the start of the campaign and ... why would that be the case? If I want to play a Hyde who doesn't have a strong Mental focus why do I have to play multiple sessions before that becomes a reality?<br /> <br /> If alternative character creation methods are listed in the book (which you implied there were on the KS page) *fantastic*, that literally solves everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T19:37:42-07:00","id":1544526,"title":"","content":"What are these Tweaks? I haven\u2019t heard of those yet. How do they work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T20:02:13-07:00","id":1544528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544526#post1544526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are these Tweaks? I haven\u2019t heard of those yet. How do they work?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the start of a session you can swap a dot between Attributes or skills, or swap out an Edge for an equivalent. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T20:09:05-07:00","id":1544530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544528#post1544528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the start of a session you can swap a dot between Attributes or skills, or swap out an Edge for an equivalent.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think that\u2019s really cool. In almost every other game, when you make a character choice, it stays forever.<br /> <br /> Does Curseborne have non-linear experience costs for increasing attributes and skills? If so, it seems like the Tweak system could be exploited.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T03:42:02-07:00","id":1544540,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah it's a great system for what I assume its purpose is, which as you say seems to be preventing people from being locked into choices permanently. (I think either CofD or Exalted Essence had similar rules).<br /> <br /> What I don't think it's good for is as an intended part of the character creation process.<br /> <br /> And no XP costs are linear so you can't exploit it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T05:18:35-07:00","id":1544543,"title":"","content":"The character creation process still provides you with options. Then, as you get familiar with the world and your character, you adjust them further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T11:39:57-07:00","id":1544581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544543#post1544543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character creation process still provides you with options. Then, as you get familiar with the world and your character, you adjust them further.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I get that.<br /> <br /> But ignoring for a moment the fact that there's apparently a completely different way of assigning Attributes and Skills also supported by the book (this is a good thing, the Storyguide chapter is the right place for it, and it solves the problem <b>completely</b>), the fact that you can change your stats gradually during play isn't particularly relevant to character creation.<br /> <br /> The fact that if I want to play a Hyde with no Mental Attributes greater than 2 I can <i>eventually</i> achieve that after spending three sessions moving dots away from where I was forced to put them into the places I wanted them to be in the first place doesn't change the fact that the system initially forced me to put dots in places I didn't want them.<br /> <br /> The fact that free distribution is also an option *does* change that fact. Which is why I don't think it's a problem as long as that option is there. But it seems odd to me to cite the Tweak system as being a way to customise your starting character when that doesn't seem to be what it's for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T13:15:39-07:00","id":1544585,"title":"","content":"While the problem that Nobody Special pointed out is certainly real, having both the Role Path and Tweaks does a lot to mitigate the issue. I might still prefer distribution but it\u2019s more minor than I first thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T17:55:34-07:00","id":1544610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544585#post1544585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the problem that Nobody Special pointed out is certainly real, having both the Role Path and Tweaks does a lot to mitigate the issue. I might still prefer distribution but it\u2019s more minor than I first thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Role Path helps if you effectively treat it as four Attributes and three Skills you can put wherever you like but that seems (and this was kind of the point of the OP) to be going against the intent of the system.<br /> <br /> Tweaks help in the sense that whatever distribution of Attributes and Skills you start with you can change it eventually but I'm afraid I will die on the hill of them not being a good answer to customisation at character creation. If what's good about Tweaks is that you can eventually achieve the same result free distribution would give you anyway, that's a strong case for free distribution just being better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T18:08:29-07:00","id":1544611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544610#post1544610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Role Path helps if you effectively treat it as four Attributes and three Skills you can put wherever you like but that seems (and this was kind of the point of the OP) to be going against the intent of the system.<br /> <br /> Tweaks help in the sense that whatever distribution of Attributes and Skills you start with you can change it eventually but I'm afraid I will die on the hill of them not being a good answer to customisation at character creation. If what's good about Tweaks is that you can eventually achieve the same result free distribution would give you anyway, that's a strong case for free distribution just being better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I basically agree. Role Paths and Tweaks mitigate the problem, but they don\u2019t entirely eliminate it. The attributes from minor and major lineage and family paths is convoluted. Like you said before, not at all transparent. <br /> <br /> Personally, I would prefer the option I mentioned in the other thread: 18 points to distribute with maximum of 9 and minimum of 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T18:17:18-07:00","id":1544613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544611#post1544611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I basically agree. Role Paths and Tweaks mitigate the problem, but they don\u2019t entirely eliminate it. The attributes from minor and major lineage and family paths is convoluted. Like you said before, not at all transparent.<br /> <br /> Personally, I would prefer the option I mentioned in the other thread: 18 points to distribute with maximum of 9 and minimum of 3.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're in luck because it sounds like that option or a similar one will be in the book which honestly is the best of both worlds solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T06:13:23-07:00","id":1544720,"title":"","content":"Storyguide Chapter is out and as promised it does indeed have rules for using Free Assignment of Attributes and Skills.<br /> <br /> I'm incredibly glad these rules are *in there* but - and I'll be honest this is partly an issue I've been having with the StoryXing Advice chapters in OP/WW games for pretty much thirty years, I do find the tone a little bit condescending.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Untethered Attribute Dots: Similarly, some players might prefer to simply have a pool of Attribute dots instead of having them assigned by Path choice. <b>There\u2019s a possibility using this method will result in characters who can\u2019t actually accomplish things their characters should be good at</b>, but if you and your players prefer a more freeform option, you can ignore the Attribute dots awarded by minor and major Paths and simply let the player allocate an additional 18 dots after putting 1 in each Attribute. </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Literally the whole reason I'd want to use Untethered Attribute Dots is that I want my character to actually be able to accomplish things she should be good at. The current system is not actually effective at letting characters accomplish things they should be good at unless you assume that what a character should be good at is <i>overwhelmingly</i> determined by which Family you pick.<br /> <br /> A Spawn of Vodnik, under the current rules, could be a Deep One who runs a used bookstore or a Selkie who is also a Navy SEAL (honestly didn't intend the pun but I stand by it). Under the default system, the game considers it safe to assume that those two characters &quot;should be good at&quot; mostly the same things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T06:39:31-07:00","id":1544722,"title":"","content":"What are you using to quantify what \u201cshould be good at\u201d means?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T07:35:00-07:00","id":1544724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZakRulz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544722#post1544722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you using to quantify what \u201cshould be good at\u201d means?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm taking it to mean &quot;things you would intuitively expect that character to be good at given their life experiences and what they do habitually, professionally, or otherwise on a day-to-day basis&quot; or possibly &quot;things that I anticipate wanting to attempt in the game that I will feel my character is not functioning properly if they do not generally perform well at.&quot;<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> If you mean how am I quantifying it *mechanically*, roughly the same way the devs are. Which is to say by dividing areas of activity onto Mental, Physical and Social and assigning more dice to the arena which you think should be strongest and fewer dice to the area you think should be weakest. More specifically, and calling right back to something Don'tEatRawHaggis said in their reply above, I'll be wanting to make sure that I have at least 5-6 dice (preferably closer to 7 or8) in pools I expect to be rolling regularly and ideally also to have pools no better than 2-3 in things I want to be notable areas of weakness for my character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-25-2024, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T20:48:57-07:00","id":1544772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544720#post1544720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Storyguide Chapter is out and as promised it does indeed have rules for using Free Assignment of Attributes and Skills.<br /> <br /> I'm incredibly glad these rules are *in there* but - and I'll be honest this is partly an issue I've been having with the StoryXing Advice chapters in OP/WW games for pretty much thirty years, I do find the tone a little bit condescending.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is an odd thing to say. The things that a character are supposed to be good at are the things that a player wants them to be good at. If a player wants a Get of Lyka who is a brilliant scientist (with appropriate attributes and skills) but has no combat ability and low physical attributes, then that is how that character is supposed to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T04:44:46-07:00","id":1544788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sergeant Brother</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544772#post1544772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that is an odd thing to say. The things that a character are supposed to be good at are the things that a player wants them to be good at. If a player wants a Get of Lyka who is a brilliant scientist (with appropriate attributes and skills) but has no combat ability and low physical attributes, then that is how that character is supposed to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read charitably, it's a sincere warning that if you super min-max your character (like if you play a character with 5 / 5 / 5 physicals, Ranged Combat 5, Close Combat 5) you'll probably leave gaps although even then somebody who's doing that level of bad-faith min-maxing probably knows what they're doing.<br /> <br /> And even then it just tars those of us who don't want our character concepts to be so heavily constrained by the Path system with the same brush. Like it basically assumes we're either not smart enough to build characters properly or intentionally trying to break the system.<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Also, I think it's worth pointing out that it's not even consciously against type characters that are hard to make in the base system.<br /> <br /> If I want to make a Maven, the Dead whose Urge seems to be thrills and new experiences, who is into fast cars and extreme sports, that's actually pretty hard to do under the system as written because the Family has an intense baked-in Social skew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","user":"Nobody Special","date":". 10-26-2024, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T07:43:24-07:00","id":1544793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nobody Special</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544459-are-you-meant-to-care-what-your-stats-are?p=1544724#post1544724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...<br /> <br /> If you mean how am I quantifying it *mechanically*, roughly the same way the devs are. Which is to say by dividing areas of activity onto Mental, Physical and Social and assigning more dice to the arena which you think should be strongest and fewer dice to the area you think should be weakest. More specifically, and calling right back to something Don'tEatRawHaggis said in their reply above, I'll be wanting to make sure that I have at least 5-6 dice (preferably closer to 7 or8) in pools I expect to be rolling regularly and ideally also to have pools no better than 2-3 in things I want to be notable areas of weakness for my character.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Apologies for the delayed response, I haven\u2019t had time to sit down and write this out until now.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Can we create both a Deep One who runs a bookstore and Navy SEAL Spawn of Vodnik who are good at their respective professions and different from each other? As you mentioned we\u2019re looking for a minimum dice pool of 5-6, preferably 7-8, for what they are \u201cgood\u201d at. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">First some probability math. Using </span></span><a href=\"https://thecontractrpg.com/info/probability/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155cc\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>https://thecontractrpg.com/info/probability/</u></span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> to determine the chance of a single hit on a roll, we determine how many d10s it takes to hit a percentage chance of a hit. For the sake of ease I\u2019ll be rounding to the nearest tenth and only include percentages over 50%</span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3d10 65.7% 1 hit</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4d10 76.0% 1 hit</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">5d10 83.1% 1 hit, 59.1% 2 hits</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">6d10 88.2% 1 hit, 68.1% 2 hits</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">7d10 91.8% 1 hit, 75.3% 2 hits, 52.9% 3 hits</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">8d10 94.2% 1 hit, 81.1% 2 hits, 61.3% 3 hits</span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To put those percentages into real world numbers I\u2019m going to use a few sports ball statistics. In the NFL Drew Breese holds the single season completion percentage for a QB at 74.4%. The WNBA all time leading scorer Diana Taurasi\u2019s best season field goal percentage is 46.1% (49.4% was her best NCAA year). I feel safe to say any dice pool above 50% counts as good and anything over 75% is very good, which is why I added the pool of 3 &amp; 4.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now, to keep with your dice pool range of 5-8 I\u2019m going to shoot for each character to have at least one thing at 8 dice, another at 7, and then a handful more between the 5-6 range. We\u2019ll start with Lineage and work through the character creation process to see how things shape up.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Primal</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For the Deep One I\u2019m going minor path for Lineage, major path for the SEAL. Our Deep One gets 3 dots between Athletics, Close Combat, and Survival while the SEAL gets 6. I\u2019m going with an equal spread here, 1 dot each for the Deep One, 2 each for the SEAL. Minor Primal attribute split is 1/2/1 with major being 3/4/3. The Deep One I\u2019ll go 1 Intelect, 1 Dexterity, 1 Stamina, 1 Presence, the SEAL 1 each Mental and Social, giving Dex 2 and the rest of the Physical 1.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deep One</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 1, Close Combat 1, Survival 1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelect 2, Cunning 1, Resolve 1, Might 1, Dexterity 2, Stamina 2, Presence 2, Manipulation 1, Composure 1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">SEAL</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 2, Close Combat 2, Survival 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelect 2, Cunning 2, Resolve 2, Might 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2, Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With just one path we\u2019ve got our SEAL with 3 pools of 4-5.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spawn of Vodnik</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deep One goes major here getting 6 dots between Esoterica, Larceny, Ranged Combat, SEAL getting 3. For the Deep One I\u2019ll leaning heavily into Esoterica with 4, Larceny and Ranged Combat getting 1 each. The SEAL doesn\u2019t really need Esotrica so instead I\u2019m going 1 Larceny and 2 Ranged Combat. Attributes the Deep One gets Mental 3, Physical 3, Social 4 while the SEAL gets Mental 2, Social 2. Yes this means at this point in time the Deep One is going to have one more Physical Dot while the SEAL has an extra Mental dot. There\u2019s still another path to pick so calm down. For the Deep One I\u2019ll do and even split Mental and Physical, 1,1,2 Social. The Seal is going Cunning/Resolve and 2 into Composure.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Deep One</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 1, Close Combat 1, Esoterica 4, Larceny 1, Ranged Combat 1, Survival 1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelect 3, Cunning 2, Resolve 2, Might 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3, Presence 3, Manipulation 2, Composure 3</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Deep One is now 6-7 dice pool for Estorica, 3-4 dice every other skill</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">SEAL</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 2, Close Combat 2, Larceny 1, Ranged Combat 2, Survival 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intellect 2, Cunning 3, Resolve 3, Might 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 2, Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 4</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">4 Skills have a pool ranging from 4-6</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Role Path</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lets just use what\u2019s in the book instead of coming up with unique paths here, I\u2019ve got a laser tattoo removal appointment to get to. While Academic or Student could work for the Deep One, Occultist is the thematically obvious choice, gaining 3 dots between Athletics, Esoterica, and Medicine and Mental 2, Physical 1, Social 1. I\u2019m going to split them 1 to Atheltics and 2 into Medicine, splitting Mental between Intellect/Cunning, Stamina (book store owners often are on their feet all day), Presence (make that sale). The SEAL really could go either way between Enforcer or Hunter, but I\u2019m going to go with Criminal cause I\u2019m cynical like that. So there\u2019s Close Combat, Larceny, and Pilot getting an equal split. Putting 1 Mental into Resolve, splitting the physical between Might and Stamina, and adding another to Composure.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 2, Close Combat 1, Esoterica 4, Larceny 1, Medicine 2, Ranged Combat 1, Survival 1</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intelect 4, Cunning 3, Resolve 2, Might 2, Dexterity 3, Stamina 4, Presence 4, Manipulation 2, Composure 3</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Esoterica Intellect/Stamina/Presence dice pool ranges 6-8, Athletics and Medicine 4-6, all others 3-5</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">SEAL</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Athletics 2, Close Combat 3, Larceny 2, Pilot 1, Ranged Combat 2, Survival 2</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Intellect 2, Cunning 3, Resolve 4, Might 3, Dexterity 3, Stamina 3, Presence 2, Manipulation 2, Composure 5</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Close Combat + Composure pool 8, CC + Resolve pool 7, CC+Physical 6</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now the Deep One has our 8 dice pool in Esoterica + Intellect, which is arguably the main pool we\u2019d look for here. Our Paths didn\u2019t give the character Enigmas which is the Skill I\u2019d argue is second behind Esoterica for our bookstore owner, so I\u2019ll put 2 of the freebie Skills there and split the other 2 between Culture and Science. The Intellect of 4 covers getting and handful of dice pools in the 5-6 range.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The SEAL needs a little more work. We\u2019ve got the handful in the 5-6 as everything except Pilot + Physical ends up there. Going 2 Close Combat and 2 Ranged Combat give a 7 and 8 dice pool for combat skills, which is what most folks think of when they think of SEALs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So there we have 2 characters same Lineage and Family, who are both sort of good at several of the same things but excel in different places.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25049-zakrulz","name":"ZakRulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25049_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T09:11:11-07:00","id":1544796,"title":"","content":"Thanks for putting the numbers together, I'm about to get extremely nitpicky but I want to highlight upfront that I actually do appreciate you engaging with this.<br /> <br /> First nitpick: you can't roll Combat Skill + Composure in SPU. Or rather you can because you can houserule it but the official rule is that close combat is Might and ranged combat is Dex. This is a change from older editions. This makes the Navy SEAL worse in a fight than the average beat cop going by the Ashcan stats (Physical stat 3 plus combat stat 2). I appreciate you've used sportsball statistics to get a sense of what dice pools &quot;should&quot; be, but that's quite misleading because we don't actually know what the &quot;difficulty&quot; of those sporting feats is.<br /> <br /> The next set of nitpicks aren't actually nitpicks so much as me unpacking why I found the original quote condescending.<br /> <br /> You've successfully demonstrated that you the system as written lets you build characters who are good at the things <i>the game designers</i> think those characters should be good at.<br /> <br /> But (and this isn't your fault because I can't expect you to be psychic) you've also kind of demonstrated that it does a terrible job at the things *I* think those characters should be good at.<br /> <br /> The Deep One Rare Book Dealer has a good pool for Esoterica + Intellect, but no dots in Artistry or Culture, both of which are things I think are important for being a rare book dealer (I've got four discretionary points to play with, but we're looking at how well just the paths work). Their physical stats are lower than I'd like (I tend to imagine Deep Ones as being *superhumanly* strong) and their social Attributes are far too good. I don't need them to be able to fire a gun at all but they have to if they take Family Primary (which they need to if they want to be able to breathe underwater).<br /> <br /> The Selkie Navy SEAL can do some of the things I'd consider necessary for the character as I'd actually want to play it, but not all of them (and again that's the outcome that the book is warning me will happen if I *don't* use their system). A huge part of being a Selkie is hanging out by the water's edge and luring people to watery graves, which I have no ability to do whatsoever with no good social stat except Composure. The Selkie doesn't need Larceny or Pilot, or Resolve 4 really (remember that the devs have said multiple times that you shouldn't be looking at what the dot ratings &quot;mean&quot; you should think of them as abstract qualities that just do what the dice do).<br /> <br /> Once again I really am appreciative that you took the time to do a worked example but ultimately the question here is whether the existing system of locking most things to Paths is a more effective way of making characters that are good at the things I want them to be good at than letting me just put those points where I want and it's borderline logically impossible for that to be the case.<br /> <br /> Even if I happened to come up with a character concept that we both agreed was perfectly reflected by the Path system, all that would mean that the Paths were <i>as good</i> as letting me free-assign. The core system really does have strengths--it's quick, it's thematic, it justifies the &quot;storypath&quot; branding and it's useful for people who find just being handed a lot of abstract numbers overwhelming and don't want to make a bajillion fiddly decisions.<br /> <br /> But it's honestly *weird* for the devs to claim that it will somehow lead to characters that do the things I want those characters to do better than letting me design the characters myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28625-nobody-special","name":"Nobody Special","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-04T02:17:59-08:00","id":1545287,"title":"","content":"I like the free form way it works a lot more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}